  And of course it meant that l didn't see the revealer but since I had gotten all the theme entries, I can't claim it would have helped.

@Andrzej

The term BASE HIT is actually somewhat redundant. If you hit a ball in such a way that you reach base—any base—it’s a hit. It’s also a BASE HIT. 

Some would argue that a home run is a hit but not a base hit because you don’t stop at any base. but I think that’s splitting hairs. If an announcer says that a batter has had five consecutive BASE HITS, (or “he has reached base five consecutive times’)I don’t think that precludes a homer or two being among them.

